  <string name="tile_label">ShutUp</string>
  <string name="about">Devices sold in some regions force the camera shutter sound to play even in silent mode. This app uses Shizuku to switch that enforcement (AudioSystem FOR_SYSTEM) off and back on.</string>
  <string name="caveats">The change lives in audioserver only: a reboot or an audioserver restart puts the device default back, and nothing else does. Uninstalling the app does not undo it, so restore before removing the app.\n\nWith the enforcement off, the shutter follows the ringer mode: it is silenced in silent or vibrate mode only. Other sounds that use the enforced stream are affected the same way.\n\nRespect the privacy of the people around you and the rules where you live.</string>
